<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Suppose for contradiction that there are only finitely many primes $p_1, \ldots , p_n$. Let $N = p_1 \cdots p_n + 1$. Then $N$ is not divisible by any $p_i$, a contradiction. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>